Subject: [PATCH 09486/11362] Ledger-invariant lint: regression lock for
 truthful archival (REQ-CONDUCTOR-ARCHIVE-2)

Conversion 1 of docs/research-notes/cumulative-coherence-rule-to-check-2026-08-21.md.

scripts/research_complete_ledger_lint.py refuses a commit whose staged
research-complete.yaml shows the archiver fix (87f209cdcf) regressing:
a NEW duplicate milestone id, the retired 'OK (conductor)' literal, or
an OK row whose deliverable does not exist. Forward-only from
2026-08-22, so the historical corpus (13 duplicate ids / 1,841 surplus
entries, 57 distinct phantom OK rows) never blocks a commit; repair of
history stays an operator decision. --report-historical is the
evidence mode: over the real ledger it counts 13 duplicate ids, 17,874
retired-literal rows, 1,496 OK rows with missing deliverables.

Fail-closed: an unparseable ledger and an entry with no completed date
both fail the lint, with reasons in comments per the QA-Layer rule.
Classified in GUARD_TARGETS (it decides whether the planner's failure
record may change). Mutations: dedup disabled -> RED, existence check
disabled -> RED, retired-literal check disabled -> RED; restored GREEN
(10 tests). Real-corpus default mode: 0 violations, 1.1s.

Also: determination-preservation-lint hook now runs under
.venv/bin/python. adversarial_verify.py imports carnot.terminal_artifacts
(landed today in conductor commits); under system python3 the lint
fail-closed refused every commit that staged a results/*.json file.

The spec.md edit (REQ-CONDUCTOR-ARCHIVE-2 section) is deliberate; the
test-suite mutation marker that flagged it was removed on purpose per
the guard's intended-change flow.

